        {
          "id": 2930808212,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "With RHEL8 GCC8.5.0 i see this kind of errors after this change:\n\n```\nepan/dissectors/packet-ip.c: In function ‘dissect_ipopt_cipso’:\nepan/dissectors/packet-ip.c:1138:61: error: ‘%u’ directive output may be truncated writing between 1 and 10 bytes into a region of size between 6 and 10 [-Werror=format-truncation=]\n             snprintf(cat_str_tmp, USHRT_MAX_STRLEN * 2, \"%u-%u\",\n                                                             ^~\nepan/dissectors/packet-ip.c:1138:57: note: directive argument in the range [0, 2147483647]\n             snprintf(cat_str_tmp, USHRT_MAX_STRLEN * 2, \"%u-%u\",\n                                                         ^~~~~~~\nepan/dissectors/packet-ip.c:1138:13: note: ‘snprintf’ output between 4 and 17 bytes into a destination of size 12\n             snprintf(cat_str_tmp, USHRT_MAX_STRLEN * 2, \"%u-%u\",\n             ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n                        cat_high, cat_low);\n                        ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n```\n\nNot sure if this is some kind false positive or not..",
          "author": {
            "id": 6524193,
            "username": "oakimk",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Joakim Karlsson",
